msgid "A missing derived artefact is a tracked gap, not a silent omission. The document stays in uploads/ until the gap closes."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:226
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A QA sidecar of general document ingestion, drained slowly. Nothing is written to ENQUEUE a block: the queue is derived (every prose block in every declared library, minus those whose summaries.json record is a current draft or confirmation), so a promoted entry is in it the moment its blocks are. A re-ingested document whose text changed re-enters it on its own, because the record's source_hash no longer matches. What an agent doing ingestion work does here is DRAIN a few: `bun run cat summaries:next -- --n K` hands it the next K blocks with their text, it writes a short summary of each in its own words, and `bun run cat summaries:record` writes them into library/<bib-slug>/summaries.json as drafts naming the agent and its model. The block itself stays verbatim and `ingested`. A library can ask for a summary in more than one language (who-iris: the six UN languages, owner 2026-11-11): the English draft, one in the document's own language read from the source, and translations of the English into the rest, each its own narrative in the block's slot. Method: skill l1-document-ingestion, \"Summarising prose blocks\". ADVISORY, never a gate: this step does not hold up Task_Citeable, and check:l1-complete reports the backlog (`block-summaries`) without failing on it. Confirming or rejecting a draft is a person's act, in `bun run cat narratives`."
msgstr ""

