#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:243
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owner, 2026-11-11 (who-iris, card Q-ODD-1 = A, and \"add to L1 doc schema errata\"). Reading the blocks to summarise them finds errors that are in the publication itself, not in the extraction: a title that says June 2006 over an introduction that says June 2005, a Spanish edition announcing nine recommendations where the English lists ten. The block stays as printed. The agent records an erratum in library/<bib-slug>/errata.json (folio-document-errata/v1): the kind, the block or page, the words as printed, the reading the evidence supports, the evidence, and its note as a draft narrative a person confirms in `bun run cat narratives`. An extraction defect is not an erratum: it is fixed by re-deriving the entry. ADVISORY: check:l1-complete reports errata and fails only on a file that does not mean what it says. Method: skill l1-document-ingestion, \"Errata: errors in the source's own text\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:152
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn; placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:136
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn; the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:212
#. Diagram label
msgid "Publish the extracted statements with source links"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:241
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record errata in the source's own text"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:190
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the gap as a bean"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/l1-document-ingestion.bpmn:44
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs the whole pipeline from CallActivity_Basic through Task_Promote and CallActivity_PublishStatements, and then Task_SummaryQueue, where it drains a few prose blocks of the advisory summary queue, and Task_Errata, where it records errors found in the source's own text — including the theme branch, which stays in THIS lane rather than dipping into Lane_2: deciding a document is a theme source is the engine asking its author a question, not a write to the shared work plan. It does not stop at a gap: Gateway_Complete's 'gap' branch leaves this lane only for Lane_2 to record the bean, then Flow_i8 returns here at CallActivity_Derive, until Gateway_Complete says complete."
msgstr ""

